  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY NIGHT THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 326 AM CDT Wed Aug 12 2026\n\nThursday night into Friday, there is another chance of rain.\nOver IA there will be synoptic support for lift in combination\nwith the abundant surface moisture pooling ahead of a stationary\nfront that will allow for convection to develop Thursday night.\nCluster analysis of the global ensemble members is in agreement\nthat the swath of heavy rain is going to remain to the north of\nour forecast region in central IA and northern IL into northern\nIN, with a 75% chance of east central IA seeing at least 1 inch\nof rain. That being said, rain chances in our forecast region\naren\u2019t completely nil. NBM guidance indicates a 25-50% chance of\nnortheastern MO and west central IL to receive 0.25 inches of\nrain. Even lower is the chance of the St. Louis metropolitan\narea seeing more than 0.1 inches of rain being 10-20%.\n\nDespite the chances for rain Thursday night into Friday, no \nlong term heat relief is expected. Models continue to be in \nconsensus that the ridge will build north toward the end of the \nweek allowing for the hot and humid air mass to remain over the \ncentral CONUS. Looking at the end of the week, ensemble guidance\nindicates a 75-90% chance of high temperatures Friday through \nSunday being 95 F or higher, and a 60-90% chance of dewpoints \nbeing greater than 70 F. On the brighter side, ensemble guidance\nis continuing to show strong signs of a cold front moving \nthrough the region at the beginning of next week. Cluster \nanalysis is in agreement that heights will fall and bring in \nnortherly flow starting Sunday night into Monday.",
